<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48813" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θητός, ὁ</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>serf, bondsman</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῆτές τε δμῶές τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.644
				</span></i>
			; later, <i>hired labourer</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῆτά τ᾽ ἄοικον ποιεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					602
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μισθωτοὺς καὶ θῆτας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Plt.</u>
					290a
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάναυσοι καὶ θ.</span> (opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δοῦλοι</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1278a13
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> at Athens,
			members of the fourth class in the constitution of Solon, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				7.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.43
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				3.82
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάτας.</span>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῆσσα</span></b> , later 
				Att.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῆττα</span></b> , ἡ, <i>hired servant-girl</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπίκληρος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Posidipp.
				35
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. γυνή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.193
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ant.Lib.
				25.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as
			Adj.,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θητική, θῆσσα τράπεζα</span>
			<i>menial</i> fare, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἑστία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>El.</u>
					205
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
